# PENDING SCENE — not yet in tools/scenes/.
#
# check-steps requires every tools/scenes/*.steps file to have live
# legs in ALL FIVE runners, deliberately: a scene that exists but
# runs nowhere is the silent-coverage class that shipped the layout
# scene green-but-absent. This scene has a mac guest only, and the
# other backends still return the not-implemented sentinel from
# Stage::ax, so registering it now would just paint four lanes red.
#
# Move to tools/scenes/a11y.steps as part of the fan-out, together
# with the Compose/GTK/WinUI accessibility reads and the per-language
# guests. It is byte-frozen already and passes on mac today.
#
# The accessibility conformance scene. Every assertion here is read from
# the PLATFORM'S OWN accessibility tree — the one an assistive client
# walks — never from kaya's scene model. Reading the model would make
# these steps agree with themselves and prove nothing; the claim under
# test is that the native control publishes a correct accessibility
# surface without kaya synthesizing one.
settle 300

# DERIVED names: identified but deliberately unlabelled, so what the
# tree reports is whatever the control took from its own caption. This
# is the free-by-construction half of the wrap-native bet, and it is the
# half no framework that draws its own widgets gets for nothing.
expect_ax button#0 "button/Save"
expect_ax checkbox#0 "checkbox/Details"
expect_ax button#1 "button/Reset"

# AUTHORED names: a bare text field has no caption to derive from, which
# is exactly where an app must supply one.
expect_ax entry#0 "field/Full name"

# A container is a GROUP to an assistive client — the reason these props
# are universal rather than kind-scoped — and its children stay
# individually reachable. It carries an identifier but NO label on
# purpose: labelling a container collapses it into one element and hides
# everything inside it (measured; see the guest's note). So a label on a
# container is a decision to hide its contents, and this scene pins the
# unlabelled behaviour because that is the one apps want by default.
expect_ax row#0 "group/Actions"
expect_ax button#2 "button/Cancel"
expect_ax button#3 "button/OK"
